<%#
  The Connect button.

  `host` and `port` come from the connection info the kubernetes adapter
  assembles -- host from the pod's node, port from the service's NodePort.
  `proxy` comes from <pod>-secret, written by the add-proxy-to-secret init
  container, because this template cannot see the launch form: its binding has
  the connection info and the Secret's keys, and nothing else.

  Which proxy is not cosmetic. OOD ships two and they behave differently:

    /node/HOST/PORT/...   forwards the whole path. JupyterLab is told the prefix
                          via CIRRUS_BASE_URL_FILE and serves it.
    /rnode/HOST/PORT/...  strips the prefix. code-server needs that, having no
                          base-path setting of its own.

  Cross them and the session comes up blank rather than erroring, which is a
  miserable thing to debug from a browser.

  No password is posted, unlike the other CIRRUS OOD apps: OOD has already
  authenticated the user before the proxy reaches this pod, and both servers run
  with their own auth disabled. So a plain link is enough.

  If `proxy` is missing -- the init container failed, or this OOD version does not
  surface extra Secret keys -- both buttons are offered rather than raising a
  NameError and leaving the user with no way in at all.
-%>
<%- kind = (defined?(proxy) && !proxy.to_s.strip.empty?) ? proxy.to_s.strip : nil -%>
<%- if kind == "rnode" -%>
  <a class="btn btn-primary" target="_blank" href="/rnode/<%= host %>/<%= port %>/">
    <i class="fa fa-code"></i> Connect to VS Code
  </a>
<%- elsif kind == "node" -%>
  <a class="btn btn-primary" target="_blank" href="/node/<%= host %>/<%= port %>/">
    <i class="fa fa-jupyter"></i> Connect to JupyterLab
  </a>
<%- else -%>
  <a class="btn btn-primary" target="_blank" href="/node/<%= host %>/<%= port %>/">
    <i class="fa fa-jupyter"></i> Connect to JupyterLab
  </a>
  <a class="btn btn-default" target="_blank" href="/rnode/<%= host %>/<%= port %>/">
    <i class="fa fa-code"></i> Connect to VS Code
  </a>
  <p class="help-block">
    This session could not report which editor it started, so both links are
    shown — use the one matching your choice on the launch form. The other will
    load blank. (Cause: the <code>proxy</code> key was missing from this
    session's Secret.)
  </p>
<%- end -%>
